# Tests for the Unemployment module (Form 1099-G)

Run with `clerk test`. Named scopes with the concrete cases of issue #21,
worked out by hand from `catala/unemployment.catala_en`. The oracle comparison
is `make difftest SCOPE=unemployment`.

> Using Unemployment
> Using Types

## Helper: a Form 1099-G

```catala
declaration scope MkG:
  input amount content money
  input repaid_in_year content money
  input repaid_before content money
  input withheld content money
  input different_state content boolean
  output form content Unemployment.Form1099G

scope MkG:
  definition form equals
    Unemployment.Form1099G {
      -- filer: Types.FilerRole.PrimaryFiler
      -- amount: amount
      -- writable_amount_paid_back_for_benefits_in_tax_year: repaid_in_year
      -- writable_amount_paid_back_for_benefits_before_tax_year: repaid_before
      -- writable_federal_tax_withheld: withheld
      -- state_is_different_state: different_state
    }
```

## Box 1 = 5,000 with 1,200 repaid in the year gives 3,800

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestRepaidInYearIsSubtracted:
  output ok condition
  g scope MkG
  u scope Unemployment.Unemployment

scope TestRepaidInYearIsSubtracted:
  definition g.amount equals $5,000
  definition g.repaid_in_year equals $1,200
  definition g.repaid_before equals $0
  definition g.withheld equals $0
  definition g.different_state equals false
  definition u.form_1099gs equals [g.form]
  assertion u.unemployment_compensation = $3,800
  assertion u.unemployment_comp_repaid_amt = $1,200
  assertion u.received_unemployment_compensation
  assertion not u.unsupported
  # known-bad outputs are rejected
  assertion u.unemployment_compensation != $5,000
  assertion u.unemployment_compensation != $6,200
  rule ok fulfilled
```

## Repayment above box 1 clamps to box 1

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestRepaymentClampsToBox1:
  output ok condition
  g scope MkG
  u scope Unemployment.Unemployment

scope TestRepaymentClampsToBox1:
  definition g.amount equals $2,000
  definition g.repaid_in_year equals $2,500
  definition g.repaid_before equals $0
  definition g.withheld equals $0
  definition g.different_state equals false
  definition u.form_1099gs equals [g.form]
  assertion u.unemployment_compensation = $0
  assertion u.unemployment_comp_repaid_amt = $2,000
  assertion u.unemployment_compensation >= $0
  rule ok fulfilled
```

## Rounding: the nets are added with cents, the sum is rounded once

Two forms of $100.40 and $100.40 total $200.80, which rounds to $201; rounding
each net first would give $200.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestSumRoundedOnce:
  output ok condition
  g1 scope MkG
  g2 scope MkG
  u scope Unemployment.Unemployment

scope TestSumRoundedOnce:
  definition g1.amount equals $100.40
  definition g1.repaid_in_year equals $0
  definition g1.repaid_before equals $0
  definition g1.withheld equals $0
  definition g1.different_state equals false
  definition g2.amount equals $100.40
  definition g2.repaid_in_year equals $0
  definition g2.repaid_before equals $0
  definition g2.withheld equals $0
  definition g2.different_state equals false
  definition u.form_1099gs equals [g1.form; g2.form]
  assertion u.unemployment_compensation = $201
  assertion u.unemployment_compensation != $200
  rule ok fulfilled
```

## Withholding flows to line 25b, rounded per form

Box 4 of $50.40 and $50.40 gives $50 + $50 = $100 (per-form rounding), not the
rounded sum $101.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestWithholdingRoundedPerForm:
  output ok condition
  g1 scope MkG
  g2 scope MkG
  u scope Unemployment.Unemployment

scope TestWithholdingRoundedPerForm:
  definition g1.amount equals $1,000
  definition g1.repaid_in_year equals $0
  definition g1.repaid_before equals $0
  definition g1.withheld equals $50.40
  definition g1.different_state equals false
  definition g2.amount equals $1,000
  definition g2.repaid_in_year equals $0
  definition g2.repaid_before equals $0
  definition g2.withheld equals $50.40
  definition g2.different_state equals false
  definition u.form_1099gs equals [g1.form; g2.form]
  assertion u.form_1099g_federal_tax_withheld = $100
  assertion u.form_1099g_federal_tax_withheld != $101
  rule ok fulfilled
```

## Knockout: prior-year repayment above $3,000

Exactly $3,000 is allowed; $3,000.01 and a total over two forms are not. An
in-year repayment never triggers it.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestRepayAt3000IsAllowed:
  output ok condition
  g scope MkG
  u scope Unemployment.Unemployment

scope TestRepayAt3000IsAllowed:
  definition g.amount equals $10,000
  definition g.repaid_in_year equals $0
  definition g.repaid_before equals $3,000
  definition g.withheld equals $0
  definition g.different_state equals false
  definition u.form_1099gs equals [g.form]
  assertion not u.ko_flow_knockout1099_g_repay_too_high
  assertion not u.unsupported
  assertion u.total_amount_paid_back_for_benefits_before_tax_year = $3,000
  rule ok fulfilled

#[test]
declaration scope TestRepayAbove3000IsKnockedOut:
  output ok condition
  g scope MkG
  u scope Unemployment.Unemployment

scope TestRepayAbove3000IsKnockedOut:
  definition g.amount equals $10,000
  definition g.repaid_in_year equals $0
  definition g.repaid_before equals $3,000.01
  definition g.withheld equals $0
  definition g.different_state equals false
  definition u.form_1099gs equals [g.form]
  assertion u.ko_flow_knockout1099_g_repay_too_high
  assertion u.unsupported
  rule ok fulfilled

#[test]
declaration scope TestRepayTotalOverTwoFormsIsKnockedOut:
  output ok condition
  g1 scope MkG
  g2 scope MkG
  u scope Unemployment.Unemployment

scope TestRepayTotalOverTwoFormsIsKnockedOut:
  definition g1.amount equals $10,000
  definition g1.repaid_in_year equals $0
  definition g1.repaid_before equals $2,000
  definition g1.withheld equals $0
  definition g1.different_state equals false
  definition g2.amount equals $10,000
  definition g2.repaid_in_year equals $9,000
  definition g2.repaid_before equals $1,500
  definition g2.withheld equals $0
  definition g2.different_state equals false
  definition u.form_1099gs equals [g1.form; g2.form]
  assertion u.ko_flow_knockout1099_g_repay_too_high
  assertion u.unsupported
  rule ok fulfilled

#[test]
declaration scope TestDifferentStateIsKnockedOut:
  output ok condition
  g scope MkG
  u scope Unemployment.Unemployment

scope TestDifferentStateIsKnockedOut:
  definition g.amount equals $1,000
  definition g.repaid_in_year equals $0
  definition g.repaid_before equals $0
  definition g.withheld equals $0
  definition g.different_state equals true
  definition u.form_1099gs equals [g.form]
  assertion u.ko_flow_knockout_unemployment_compensation_unsupported_state
  assertion not u.ko_flow_knockout1099_g_repay_too_high
  assertion u.unsupported
  rule ok fulfilled

#[test]
declaration scope TestNoForms:
  output ok condition
  u scope Unemployment.Unemployment

scope TestNoForms:
  definition u.form_1099gs equals []
  assertion u.unemployment_compensation = $0
  assertion not u.received_unemployment_compensation
  assertion not u.unsupported
  rule ok fulfilled
```
